 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per sample, same as the base SDF evaluation. The cost is dominated by the arithmetic operations of the inverse transform (matrix-vector multiplication or trigonometric functions).
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$. No additional memory is required for geometry or transformation matrices beyond the parameters passed to the shader/function.
-- **Performance:** Highly efficient for instancing and animation. Transformations are computed per-ray-sample, allowing for dynamic animation (e.g., twisting, bending) without CPU-side updates.
